{"id":"s3.6.2","slug":"derivatives","title":"Derivatives","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">Derivative problems on the test almost always involve the power rule for polynomials. For a term $ax^n$, its derivative is $anx^{n-1}$. To find the derivative of a polynomial, apply this rule to each term.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For $f(x) = x^3 - 3x^2 + x - 3$, the first derivative is $f'(x) = 3x^2 - 6x + 1$. To find the second derivative, $f''(x)$, simply differentiate $f'(x)$: $f''(x) = 6x - 6$.</p><p class=\"mb-4\">Occasionally, derivatives of other functions like sin, cos, e^x, and ln x are needed, especially for L'Hôpital's rule.</p>","summary":"Derivative problems on the test almost always involve the power rule for polynomials.","generation_guideline":"Generate a problem asking for the first or second derivative of a polynomial at a given point.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"If $f(x) = 3x^2 + x - 5$, find $f'(-2)$.","answer":"-11","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":2,"text":"If $f(x) = x^2 - 2x + 22$, find $f'(2)$.","answer":"2","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":3,"text":"If $g(x) = 2x^2 - 3x + 1$, find $g'(2)$.","answer":"5","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":4,"text":"If $f(x) = 3x^3 - 3x + 3$, find $f'(-3)$.","answer":"78","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":5,"text":"If $f(x) = 4x^3 + 2x^2$, find $f''(-0.5)$.","answer":"-8","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":6,"text":"If $f(x) = x^3 - 3x + 3$, find $f'(3)$.","answer":"24","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":7,"text":"If $f(x) = x^4 - 4x + 4$, find $f'(4)$.","answer":"252","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":8,"text":"If $f(x) = 3x^2 + 4x - 5$, find $f'(-6)$.","answer":"-32","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":9,"text":"If $f(x) = 2x^3 - 3x^4$, find $f'(-1)$.","answer":"18","kind":"exact","tags":["functions","calculus"]},{"id":10,"text":"If $f(x) = 4x^3 - 3x^2 + 1$, find $f'(-